 ### Tangible Dataset Manipulation
-A technique where rotating a physical reference object (shaped as a cuboctahedron) rotates the corresponding virtual volume dataset, providing natural 6 DOF interaction [S2]. It is chosen when natural, bare-hand exploration of volume orientation is preferred over precise digital control. It differs from standard object manipulation by using a physical reference object observed through a handheld tablet window for tracking rather than a depth ray [S2].
